Subject: [PATCH] ipa: libipa: camera_sensor_helper: add imx681

TEMPLATE, NOT APPLIABLE YET. The analogue gain law of the IMX681 is not known (REA
question G1 in hardware/cameras/evidence/2026-10-31-quality-parity.md). Windows only
shows that the gain is a linear register code (MIPI CCS 0x0204); the divisor is not in
the module data. Replace @IMX681_GAIN_DIV@ and @IMX681_BLACK16@ and save as
libcamera-sp11-imx681-helper.patch (an unfilled template must never be applied: with a
wrong divisor the Software ISP AGC range is wrong).

  @IMX681_GAIN_DIV@  gain = code / DIV (CCS linear model, c0 = 0): integer
  @IMX681_BLACK16@   black level in the 16 bit scale: (10 bit black level) << 6

Without the helper libcamera logs "Failed to create camera sensor helper for imx681"
and uses the control value as the gain; capture works, AGC is coarse.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
---
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -/* anchor: insert before the "class CameraSensorHelperOv13858" definition */
+class CameraSensorHelperImx681 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperImx681()
+	{
+		blackLevel_ = @IMX681_BLACK16@;
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, @IMX681_GAIN_DIV@ };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx681", CameraSensorHelperImx681)
+
